"modal-deduction","level":"B2","prompt":"The evidence is inconclusive; this is only possible: “They ____ be restoring the old portrait.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"have to"},{"id":"B","text":"might"},{"id":"C","text":"must"},{"id":"D","text":"cannot"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"The prompt says **possible but uncertain**.","explanation":"**Might** leaves the action possible without claiming certainty.","keywords":["uncertain-possibility"],"skill":"uncertain-possibility","contextKey":"modal-deduction-2","fingerprint":"7ee0a9621f4744823c4767236da3e675f1720855627dd5dca0ae6bc7f0a5d24d","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-deduction"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The prompt says **possible but uncertain**.","**Might** leaves the action possible without claiming certainty.","Choose **might**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Have to ordinarily introduces a requirement here, not the requested uncertain possibility.","B":"**Might** leaves the action possible without claiming certainty.","C":"Must would express a stronger positive conclusion than the prompt supports.","D":"Cannot rules the action out."}}},{"id":"826a3ddc-6079-5e87-a0c7-120b3dd10afe","topicSlug":"modal-deduction","level":"B2","prompt":"Build a deduction about an action happening now: “She must ____ the old portrait.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"be restoring"},{"id":"B","text":"restoring"},{"id":"C","text":"is restoring"},{"id":"D","text":"been restoring"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"A present ongoing deduction has the form **modal + be + -ing**.","explanation":"After must, use **be + restoring** for an ongoing action.","keywords":["deduction-continuous-form"],"skill":"deduction-continuous-form","contextKey":"modal-deduction-2","fingerprint":"1e0223c877759eab24a4af51a8dfadf1ccfcc7ab7c2347a8e29215b14deac59f","sour