ng positive conclusion requested.","D":"Must not normally conveys prohibition, not a positive deduction."}}},{"id":"d1f2ea97-351e-5a5e-adbd-8c4d2d70c75a","topicSlug":"modal-deduction","level":"B2","prompt":"The evidence rules this out as impossible: “They ____ be measuring the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"may"},{"id":"B","text":"must not"},{"id":"C","text":"cannot"},{"id":"D","text":"must"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Choose the modal for an **impossible explanation**, not a prohibition.","explanation":"**Cannot** expresses impossibility according to the stated evidence.","keywords":["impossibility"],"skill":"impossibility","contextKey":"modal-deduction-3","fingerprint":"555ec3c5ea684a56d2d8afe34019fce99e7962358e2809f2922175490a49ae2e","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-deduction"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Choose the modal for an **impossible explanation**, not a prohibition.","**Cannot** expresses impossibility according to the stated evidence.","Choose **cannot**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"May would leave the event possible.","B":"Must not normally prohibits an action rather than ruling it out as impossible.","C":"**Cannot** expresses impossibility according to the stated evidence.","D":"Must would give a strong positive conclusion."}}},{"id":"4b3db3c2-1089-570d-a4fb-c3c29ef61b90","topicSlug":"modal-deduction","level":"B2","prompt":"The evidence is inconclusive; this is only possible: “They ____ be measuring the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"must"},{"id":"B","text":"cannot"},{"id":"C","text":"have to"},{"id":"D","text":"might"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"The prompt says **possible but uncertain**.","explanation":"**Might** leaves the action possible without claiming certainty.","keywords":["uncertain-possibility"],"skill":"unce